 "verdict": "Consumption is normal to slightly high. With the hours from all cameras combined, from 2 Aug to 9 Oct the machines received 5,771 L; their running hours (about 256 machine-hours) need about 5,607 L, so about 164 L (3%) more was delivered than the hours explain — within the margin of error. That is 22.6 L per machine-hour against about 22 expected. Two periods stand out: 18–24 Aug (+152 L, 28.8 L/h) and 18–24 Sep (+193 L, 31 L/h); both include days when D1 up was off, so their hours are estimates from D2. Diesel delivered to the Komatsu is carried by jerrycan to the Hitachi, so per-machine figures are misleading; the total is the reliable figure. The jerrycans are the weak point.",
 "expected": "Expected: Hitachi with breaker 24 L/h (20–28), Komatsu 17 L/h (14–20). Hours from all cameras combined; days with no camera at all (11 Aug) use the month average. One interval can be off by a whole tank (tanks are not filled to the same level each time). 8 Oct (200 L) and 9 Oct (495 L) together: 695 L for about 633 L expected.",
 "whole": "18 Apr – 9 Oct: 16,478 L for 4,500 m³ excavated = 3.66 L/m³ (contract table assumed 3.07).",
